{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Information.HeckeLogDecomposition"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MagicShell.deltaCouplingSubstrateForm_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MagicShell.deltaCouplingSubstrateForm_canonical","kind":"instance","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MagicShell/DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.lean#L98-L128","doc":"Canonical concrete instance of `DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm` for any\n    Wenzl-regime `(q, m_e)`.\n\nThe instance discharges the class abstraction by *defining*\n`delta_coupling Z N` to be the closed-form expression\n`(A - 2) · E_0 · log(1/(q - q⁻¹))`. The `closed_form` field is then\nsatisfied by `rfl`. The empirical claim — that this closed form matches\nthe AME-extracted magic-shell stabilisation — remains the conjectural\ncontent (verified at the (Z,N)=(2,2) anchor with 0.71% gap).\n\nConstruction:\n  q0 := q                              (substrate parameter, q > 1)\n  m_e := m_e                           (any positive value)\n  E_0 := m_e / (q (q - 1))             (Hecke energy unit)\n  delta_coupling Z N := ((Z+N) - 2) · E_0 · log(1/(q - q⁻¹))\n  closed_form := rfl                   (definitional)\n\nRef: probe_delta_coupling_leading_form.py (numerical witness at q_0, ⁴He).\nRef: docs/audits/2026-05-17-delta-coupling-substrate-derivation.md\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MagicShell.delta_coupling_two_forms_equivalent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MagicShell.delta_coupling_two_forms_equivalent","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MagicShell/DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.lean#L79-L96","doc":"The substrate-derivation form is algebraically equivalent to the\nskein-convention leading form by the log decomposition\n(`prop:hecke-log-decomposition`). For every (Z, N) at the magic-\nshell anchor, the skein-form expression\n    (A - 2) · E_0 · log(1/(q_0 - q_0⁻¹))\nequals the thermodynamic-form expression\n    (A - 2) · E_0 · [log(1/((q_0-1)/q_0)) - log(1 + q_0)]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MagicShell.delta_coupling_substrate_at_2_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MagicShell.delta_coupling_substrate_at_2_2","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MagicShell/DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.lean#L64-L77","doc":"The closed-form holds at the doubly-magic anchor (Z, N) = (2, 2) for\n⁴He within 0.71% of the AME-extracted +13.20 MeV. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MagicShell/DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The closed-form claim: Δ_coupling(Z, N) = (A-2) · E_0 · log(1/h(q_0)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.delta_coupling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.delta_coupling","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MagicShell/DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The Δ_coupling value at magic shell (Z, N) with mass number A. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.E_0_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.E_0_def","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MagicShell/DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.lean#L56-L56","doc":"E_0 definition holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.E_0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.E_0","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MagicShell/DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The Hecke energy unit E_0 = m_e / (q_0 (q_0 - 1)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.m_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.m_e","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MagicShell/DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Electron mass m_e (CAL-1 calibration anchor). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.q0_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.q0_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MagicShell/DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.lean#L50-L50","doc":"q_0 > 1 — required for h(q_0) > 0 and log positivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.q0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.q0","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MagicShell/DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The substrate parameter q_0 (Wenzl positivity regime). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MagicShell/DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MagicShell.DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm","kind":"class","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MagicShell/DeltaCouplingSubstrateForm.lean#L33-L62","doc":"Magic-shell stabilization energy as a substrate-derived closed form.\n\nThe class encodes the conjecture that Δ_coupling at finite-A magic\nshells equals (A - 2) · E_0 · log(1/h(q_0)) — the thermodynamic free-\nenergy correction per excess nucleon pair at the QOU Hecke-thermal\nscale, in the skein-convention normalisation.\n\nFields are concrete propositional equalities asserting the closed\nform. When promoted to a theorem (post cross-anchor verification +\nLP-active-set derivation of (A-2)), the class instance becomes the\ngenuine substrate derivation. Until then it is axiomatised as a\nconjecture class per AGENTS.md §3b.\n","signatureChunk":0}]}